<h1>Claudia Zuno</h1>
<p>12th Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.claudiafor12thward.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (claudiafor12thward.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Challenging Ald. Julia Ramirez. Her top pledge is removing the concrete barriers and protected bike lanes on Archer and Kedzie avenues and finding alternatives that keep pedestrian routes safe while accommodating truck routes. She also wants to restore gunshot detection technology such as ShotSpotter, support law enforcement, and help small businesses with a chamber of commerce and access to grants and training.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Second-generation owner of Zuno Photographic, a family photography business founded in 1969; lifelong Brighton Park resident who has served with the Mexican Civic Society of Illinois, the Mexican-American Women&#39;s Auxiliary, and the National Museum of Mexican Art.</p>
